From: kaiwater <kaiwater@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sing-box: do not build the naive outbound by default

SING_BOX_BUILD_NAIVE_OUTBOUND is a def_bool y symbol, so it cannot be turned off from .config; it drags in libcronet, whose gn toolchain only supports linux/amd64. Default it off; users who need naive can still enable it explicitly on amd64 hosts.

---
diff --git a/net/sing-box/Makefile b/net/sing-box/Makefile
index 7549839..fc58e94 100644
--- a/net/sing-box/Makefile
+++ b/net/sing-box/Makefile
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ define Package/sing-box/config
   depends on $(subst @,,$(GO_ARCH_DEPENDS))
 
   config SING_BOX_BUILD_NAIVE_OUTBOUND
-  def_bool y
+  def_bool n
   depends on !(arc||armeb||loongarch64||mips||mips64||powerpc||TARGET_gemini)
 endef
 
